          "transfer": "<p>Choose the matching route. Write one task and one check before opening the example. There can be more than one useful answer.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Fresh source</th><th>Your task</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>L1-E-X</code></td><td>A book swap has eight helpers and thirty donated books. It is free, on Sunday afternoon. The location is unconfirmed.</td><td>Choose a draft you can check without inventing a location.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>",
          "comparison": "<details><summary>Compare your approach</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Everyday:</strong> “Draft an invitation. Check it says free and Sunday afternoon, and keeps the location to be confirmed.” A named library would need confirmation first.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If your answer uses a different output, keep it when the source supports it and the check can reveal a mistake. If you reused “make it good,” replace that phrase with a check of a number, claim or missing fact.</p>\n</details>",
