          "transfer": "<p>Write a two-to-four-sentence request using one of these sources. Include all four ingredients; no exact wording is required.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Fresh source</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>L2-E-X</code></td><td>A seed-swap table has six helpers and forty seed packets. It opens on Sunday for one hour. The location and start time are undecided.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>",
          "comparison": "<details><summary>Compare with a worked request</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Everyday:</strong> “Draft a short invitation to a one-hour seed swap on Sunday, with six helpers and forty packets available. Keep location and start time to be confirmed. I will check every number and avoid promising a packet to everyone, since attendance is unknown.”</li>\n</ul>\n<p>An answer is ready for the next step when the facts remain correct, the output can be inspected, uncertainty is visible and the check could catch an error. If your wording differs but achieves these, keep it. If it adds an unagreed date, place or limit, remove that invention.</p>\n</details>",
          "own": "<p>Take your Lesson 1 task. Write the request, then annotate it with <strong>context / task / shape and limits / check</strong>. If one ingredient is absent, add just the sentence needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check rubric:</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>What you should be able to point to</th><th>If it is missing</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Faithful context</td><td>Each included number, name or commitment appears in your source.</td><td>Remove or clearly label the extra detail as a suggestion.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Useful task</td><td>One draft output is named.</td><td>Replace “help me” with the draft you want.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Inspectable shape and limits</td><td>A reader can tell how to organise it and what not to guess.</td><td>Add columns, a short outline or explicit unknowns.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Meaningful check</td><td>You name what you will compare with which source.</td><td>Replace “check quality” with a specific check.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p>Keep the source beside the request. Save the version you want to work from; checking every box does not certify the answer an AI might produce.</p>\n<p><strong>Take forward:</strong> <a href=\"#lesson=3\">Lesson 3: Check an answer</a> gives you a flawed answer to inspect, so you can practise even without calling an AI tool.</p>"
